<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-indent: 0.25in; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify">Only holders of class A ordinary
shares of a nominal or par value of US$0.0001 each (each carrying one (1) vote per share) and class B ordinary shares of a nominal or
par value of US$0.0001 each (each carrying twenty (20) votes per share) of the Company (collectively, the &ldquo;Ordinary Shares&rdquo;)
registered in the register of members at the close of business on August 20, 2026 (the &ldquo;Record Date&rdquo;), can vote at the Extraordinary
Meeting or at any adjournment that may take place.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-indent: 0.25in; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify">We cordially invite all holders
of Ordinary Shares to attend the Extraordinary Meeting in person. However, holders of Ordinary Shares entitled to attend and vote are
entitled to appoint a proxy to attend and vote instead of such holders. A proxy need not be a shareholder of the Company. If you are a
holder of Ordinary Shares and whether or not you expect to attend the Extraordinary Meeting in person, please mark, date, sign and return
the enclosed form of proxy as promptly as possible to ensure your representation and the presence of a quorum at the Extraordinary Meeting.
If you send in your form of proxy and then decide to attend the Extraordinary Meeting to vote your Ordinary Shares in person, you may
still do so. Your proxy is revocable in accordance with the procedures set forth in the proxy statement. The enclosed form of proxy is
to be delivered to the attention of Mr. Qirui Dou, 7545 Irvine Center Drive, Suite 200, Irvine, CA 92618 and must arrive no later than
the time for holding the Extraordinary Meeting or any adjournment thereof.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-indent: 0.25in; margin-top: 0pt; margin-right: 0; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify">Shareholders may obtain
a copy of the proxy materials, including the Company&rsquo;s annual report on Form 20-F, from the Company&rsquo;s website at <I>https://ir.yuedaholding.com/
</I>or by submitting a request to the Investor Relations department of the Company at ir@yuedaholding.com.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

