<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>PROPOSAL 1</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: center"><B>SHARE CONSOLIDATION PROPOSAL</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Proposed Share Consolidation </B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">The Board approved, and directed
that there be submitted to the shareholders of the Company for approval, as an ordinary resolution, a share consolidation of the Company&rsquo;s
issued and unissued class A ordinary shares and class B ordinary shares at a ratio of one (1)-for-ten (10), whereby every ten (10) class
A ordinary shares of a nominal or par value of US$0.0001 each will be consolidated into one (1) class A ordinary share of a nominal or
par value of US$0.001, and every ten (10) class B ordinary shares of a nominal or par value of US$0.0001 each will be consolidated into
one (1) class B ordinary share of a nominal or par value of US$0.001.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">As a consequence of the Share
Consolidation, the Company&rsquo;s authorized share capital will be changed:</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><B>From</B>: US$40,000,000
divided into 360,000,000,000 class A ordinary shares of a nominal or par value of US$0.0001 each and 40,000,000,000 class B ordinary shares
of a nominal or par value of US$0.0001 each;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in"><B>To</B>: US$40,000,000 divided
into 36,000,000,000 class A ordinary shares of a nominal or par value of US$0.001 each and 4,000,000,000 class B ordinary shares of a
nominal or par value of US$0.001 each.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">No fractional shares will
be issued to any shareholder in connection with the Share Consolidation. Each shareholder will instead be entitled to receive one share
of the Company in lieu of the fractional share of that class that would otherwise have resulted from the Share Consolidation.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">The Share Consolidation is
expected to become effective on the date confirmed by Nasdaq or on a date to which Nasdaq has raised no objection.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Purpose of the Share Consolidation </B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">The Company&rsquo;s class
A ordinary shares are listed on Nasdaq under the trading symbol of &ldquo;YDKG&rdquo;. In order for class A ordinary shares to continue
to be listed on Nasdaq, the Company must satisfy the Listing Rules of Nasdaq. Although the Company has not yet received any letter from
Nasdaq regarding the non-compliance with the requirement to maintain a minimum closing bid price of $1.00 per share (the &ldquo;Minimum
Bid Price Requirement&rdquo;), as set forth in Nasdaq Listing Rule 5550(a)(2), in 2026 so far, the Company has been closely monitoring
the closing bid price of its class A ordinary shares. Violating the Minimum Bid Price Requirement without regaining compliance may lead
to delisting of the Company. Such potential delisting from Nasdaq and continued or further declines in the Company&rsquo;s share price
could also greatly impair its ability to raise additional necessary capital through equity or debt financing.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">To enhance the Company&rsquo;s
ability to retain compliance with the Minimum Bid Price Requirement and remain listed on Nasdaq, the Board believes that the Share Consolidation
is in the best interests of the Company and its shareholders<FONT STYLE="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">.</FONT> The Board
also believes that increasing the per-share trading price of the Company&rsquo;s class A ordinary shares may assist the Company in satisfying
the Minimum Bid Price Requirement. In addition, the Board believes that an increased market price per class A ordinary share resulting
from the Share Consolidation may improve the marketability of the class A ordinary shares and may encourage interest in the Company&rsquo;s
class A ordinary shares among certain institutional investors, analysts and brokers whose policies or practices may discourage investments
in lower-priced securities.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">As a result, the Board is
soliciting shareholders&rsquo; approval for the authorization of the Board to effect the Share Consolidation on the date confirmed by
Nasdaq or on a date to which Nasdaq has raised no objection, and to provide authorization to the Board to make all necessary filings with
Nasdaq in connection to any consolidation of the shares of the Company and to round up any fractions of shares issued to such shareholders
of the Company as a result of the Share Consolidation.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">There can be no assurance
that, after the Share Consolidation, the Company will be able to maintain the listing of class A ordinary shares on Nasdaq. Nasdaq maintains
several other continued listing requirements currently applicable to the listing of class A ordinary shares. Shareholders should recognize
that if the Share Consolidation is effected, they will own a smaller number of class A ordinary shares than they currently own. While
the Company expects that the Share Consolidation will result in an increase in the market price of class A ordinary shares, it may not
increase the market price of class A ordinary shares in proportion to the reduction in the number of class A ordinary shares outstanding
or result in a permanent increase in the market price (which depends on many factors, including but not limited to the Company&rsquo;s
performance, prospects and other factors that may be unrelated to the number of class A ordinary shares outstanding).</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B></B></P>

<!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 5; Value: 2 -->
    <DIV STYLE="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->5<!-- Field: /Sequence --></P></DIV>
    <DIV STYLE="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><P STYLE="margin: 0pt">&nbsp;</P></DIV>
    <!-- Field: /Page -->

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Effects of the Share Consolidation </B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">The Share Consolidation will
affect all shareholders uniformly, except for adjustments resulting from the treatment of fractional shares described above. Except for
such fractional-share adjustments, the Share Consolidation will not change any shareholder&rsquo;s proportionate ownership interest or
relative voting power in the Company.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">The Share Consolidation will
reduce the number of issued and outstanding Ordinary Shares at a ratio of (1)-for-ten (10) and will correspondingly increase the nominal
or par value from US$0.0001 to US$0.001 per Ordinary Share.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">Each shareholder&rsquo;s proportionate
ownership of the issued and outstanding class A ordinary shares and class B ordinary shares immediately following the effectiveness of
the Share Consolidation would remain the same, with the exception of adjustments related to the treatment of fractional shares.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">The Share Consolidation will
not affect the Company&rsquo;s obligation to publicly file financial and other information periodically with the SEC. The Share Consolidation
is not intended to be, and will not have the effect of, a &ldquo;going private transaction&rdquo; covered by Rule 13e-3 under the Exchange
Act. Historical share and per-share amounts in the Company&rsquo;s financial statements and related disclosures will be adjusted, as applicable,
to reflect the Share Consolidation.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>&nbsp;</B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Risks Associated with the Share Consolidation </B></P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">There are risks associated
with the Share Consolidation. Shareholders should note that the effect of the Share Consolidation, if any, upon the market price for the
Company&rsquo;s class A ordinary shares cannot be accurately predicted. The Company cannot assure you that the Share Consolidation will
increase, or maintain any increase in, the market price of the class A ordinary shares. The market price will continue to depend on the
Company&rsquo;s performance, market conditions and other factors unrelated to the number of shares outstanding. Some investors may view
the Share Consolidation negatively, we cannot assure you that the Share Consolidation will not adversely impact the market price of the
Company&rsquo;s class A ordinary shares.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">In addition, the aggregate
market value of the class A ordinary shares may decrease following the Share Consolidation. The Share Consolidation may reduce the number
of shareholders holding round lots of the class A ordinary shares.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify; text-indent: 0.25in">While we believe that the
Share Consolidation will be sufficient to maintain our listing on Nasdaq, it is possible that, even if the Share Consolidation results
in a closing price for the Company&rsquo;s class A ordinary shares that exceeds $1.00 per share, the Company may not be able to continue
to satisfy other criteria for continued listing of the Company&rsquo;s class A ordinary shares on Nasdaq. Although the Company believes
that it will continue satisfying all of the other continued listing criteria, the Company cannot assure you that this will be the case.</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&nbsp;</P>

<P STYLE="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><B>Full Text of the Resolution</B></P>

